[rexglue-native-monitor] SDK 0077, 2026-11-16 (the owner, 13:26: "when the application starts it'll still start on the
monitor that has the cursor then it quickly swaps to their correct monitor, we need to eliminate the need to switch").
Needs 0074: it changes 0074's lines, and 0074 was held from every release, so the two go out together.
What it does, in WindowSDL::OpenImpl, on top of 0074 (the window made centered on the chosen display):
- No display chosen (monitor_name empty and monitor 0, the defaults) or the chosen one isn't connected: a window that
  starts fullscreen (fullscreen is on by default; not with start_in_background) is made on the primary display. A
  plain window keeps the system's place.
- X11: a window that starts fullscreen gets _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN before it's mapped (AskX11FullscreenOnMap), so
  the window manager maps it fullscreen on its display at once (EWMH: the state of a window is read when it's mapped).
- Windows: the first size is taken at the content scale of the display the window is made on (SDL3 makes the process
  per-monitor DPI aware, v2), not the primary display's.
- One log line where the window showed: "window: shown at X,Y on display N[, fullscreen]".
Why: SDL resolves fullscreen against the primary display for a window made without a position, the window manager
puts such a window on the screen with the mouse (X11: no USPosition), and SDL asks for fullscreen only after the map.
So with the defaults (automatic display, fullscreen) the window was first shown as a window on the mouse's screen and
then moved fullscreen to the primary; with a display chosen and 0074 it was first shown as a plain window on its
display and filled it a moment later.
Measured on the owner's PC (X11, Muffin; DP-0 1920x1080 primary with the mouse, DP-2 1080x1920 portrait chosen; a test
window doing exactly OpenImpl's calls with the SDK's SDL 3.5.0; the X server's events and 5 ms samples): released
code, first visible on DP-0, on DP-2 5-12 ms later (with an exclusive mode it even ends fullscreen on DP-0); 0074, on
DP-2 only but a 1080x720 window for 62 ms before fullscreen; 0077, fullscreen on DP-2 from the first visible frame,
no move or resize after it. Windows (under Wine): no case ever showed on another screen, before or after.
Unchanged: start_in_background (fullscreen still waits for the first click), moving an open window from F2
(SetDisplayChoice), Wayland (fullscreen already went to the chosen output; a plain window is placed by the
compositor), macOS.

